  "id": "DrugBank_DB00902 - MONDO_7448",
  "verbalization": "Methdilazine appears to be linked to Familial Dermatographia through a chain of indications that involve Angioedema and Phenyltoloxamine. The evidence suggests that Methdilazine may act as a mediator in the pathophysiology of Familial Dermatographia, possibly by influencing the inflammatory response associated with Angioedema. This connection is supported by the shared indication of Angioedema with Phenyltoloxamine, which in turn is linked to Familial Dermatographia. The presence of multiple pathways involving different compounds—such as Tripelennamine and Phenyltoloxamine—adds to the complexity of the relationship, but all converge on the same target, Familial Dermatographia. The strength of the evidence is consistent across different paths, reinforcing the hypothesis that Methdilazine may play a role in the development of this condition through an indirect mechanism involving Angioedema.",
